 ## Background
-Tiled resources were first introduced in DirectX 11.2 (Windows 8.1) for 2D textures. Volume (3D) tiled resources were added in Direct3D 11.3 and Direct3D 12 [S1, unofficial][S2][S3]. The feature targets memory issues in high-resolution 3D texture rendering by allowing only part of the texture to be loaded onto the GPU at any given time [S1, unofficial]. It is similar to the virtual texturing used in id Tech 5 (Rage), but leverages hardware virtual addressing to reduce the CPU overhead associated with manual page management [S1, unofficial]. It is used in voxel-based rendering techniques, such as Voxel Cone Traced Global Illumination, to manage large voxel grids efficiently [S1, unofficial].
